meta {
  name: Confirm the topic placement
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/placements/{{placementId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "status": "confirmed",
    "page_end": 29
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.status: eq confirmed
  res.body.page_end: eq 29
  res.body.confirmed_by: eq {{callerPersonId}}
  res.body.confirmed_at: isDefined
}

docs {
  Confirming is the act this whole surface exists for. Until a person agrees,
  a mapping is a suggestion; afterwards it is what the school says the pupils
  are being taught from, and it is what resolution returns by default.

  confirmed_by and confirmed_at are written by the server from the token and
  refused in the body with 422. Attribution a caller could type is attribution
  nobody can rely on, and this is the field a teacher's name ends up next to.

  Moving a confirmed placement back to proposed or rejected clears both fields
  again, so a row never carries a confirmation that no longer stands.
}
